-- title:
--   Nontriviality of the auxiliary-level residual Hecke module M_L
-- statement:
--   Fix a positive integer $N$, a set $S$ of natural numbers, and a prime $r$ with $r \nmid N$. Let $\mathcal O$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain of characteristic zero, with residue field $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the anemic weight-two Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) to $k$; here that Hecke algebra is the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}\bigl(S_2(\Gamma_0(N))\bigr)$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin` attached to primes $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators `heckeULin` attached to primes $q$ with $q \mid N$ and $q \notin S$. Assume [`CuspForm.AuxLevel.OpComm N r S 𝒪`](def/CuspForm_AuxLevelHeckeModule.html#L30), i.e. that the operators `op N r S 𝒪 g`, for $g$ ranging over the index type `Gen N r S`, commute with one another. These data assemble into the Hecke data [`CuspForm.AuxLevel.heckeData N r S 𝒪 θ hc`](def/CuspForm_AuxLevelHeckeModule.html#L33) on the carrier `Carrier N r 𝒪`, whose generating set is `Gen N r S`, whose operators are the `op N r S 𝒪 g`, whose commutativity is the hypothesis, and whose residual eigenvalue system sends $g$ to $\theta$ applied to the Hecke operator [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.T`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L77) indexed by $g$. The assertion is that the associated module [`CuspForm.AuxLevel.ML N r S 𝒪 θ hc`](def/CuspForm_AuxLevelHeckeModule.html#L46) — a module over $\mathcal O$ and, compatibly, over the polynomial algebra $\mathcal O[X_g : g \in$ `Gen N r S` $]$ — is nontrivial, that is, it has two distinct elements and in particular is nonzero.
--
--   This is the occupancy statement underlying the Taylor–Wiles argument at the auxiliary level: every residual eigensystem $\theta$ of the anemic weight-two Hecke algebra of level $N$ is realised in the localised cohomology module at level divisible by the auxiliary prime $r$, the nonvanishing coming via Eichler–Shimura from the faithful action of the Hecke algebra on parabolic cohomology. It is used by the constructions of Galois representations and Taylor–Wiles modules attached to $M_L$, such as [`CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_galoisRepAdic_moduleEnd_ML_flat`](thm.html#CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_galoisRepAdic_moduleEnd_ML_flat) and [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_taylorWilesModule_of_linearEquiv_ML_flat`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_taylorWilesModule_of_linearEquiv_ML_flat).
